Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Cut trees hidden in sight as the player walks between maps
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Walking from one map into another clears the map's local flags, among
them the ones Cut sets on the trees it cuts. On the DS that's unseen:
the map's people go as the player leaves it, and a cut tree comes back
only as the player walks back in, off the DS's narrower screen. On the
3DS's wider field the maps beside the player's have their people
brought, their local flags taken as clear, and the two Cut trees on
Eterna Forest's east side came back in sight as soon as the player
stepped onto Route 205, and again as they walked back into the forest's
zone.

A map's local flags are now remembered as the player leaves it, till
they walk back in: what they hid isn't brought from beside, and walking
back in, what they hid in sight on the 3DS's screen stays hidden, its
flag set again before the map's people are made. Further away, it comes
back as on the DS, unseen.
